'''Sienar Test Facility 73''' was a [[Sienar Fleet Systems]] testing facility on the [[planet]] [[Sienar TF73]]. In [[4 BBY]], [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|stole]] a [[TIE Avenger prototype|TIE Avenger]] prototype from the facility. 

==Description==
Sienar Test Facility 73 was a testing facility operated by [[Sienar Fleet Systems]], located on the snowy [[planet]] [[Sienar TF73]]; one of the various numerically designated planets owned by the company.<ref name="Databank" /> The facility consisted of a series of connected structures and contained at least one commissary<ref name="One Year Later AD">{{Andor|One Year Later}} {{AD</ref> and at least three hangars.<ref name="One Year Later" />

==History==
By [[4 BBY]], the facility was operational, with its own workforce and a [[Sienar Test Facility 73 defense battalion|dedicated defense battalion]]<ref name="Databank" /> consisting of [[stormtrooper]]s, [[range trooper]]s and at least two [[TIE/ad v1]]s. In 4 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]], its workforce included [[Niya]], her [[Niya's coworker|coworker]], and her [[Niya's supervisor|supervisor]]. During that year, [[Niya]] assisted [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], a rebel operative posing as a [[Sienar test pilot]], in [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|stealing]] the facility's [[TIE Avenger prototype|TIE Avenger]] prototype from one of its hangars. During the theft, Andor damaged the hangar using the [[TIE series|TIE]]’s weapon systems.<ref name="One Year Later" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Sienar Test Facility 73 appeared in the [[One Year Later|first episode]] of the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', which was released on [[Disney+]]<ref name="One Year Later" /> on [[April 22]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref> The facility was first revealed prior to the release of the episode in a sizzle reel for the series exclusively shown at [[Wikipedia:D23 (Disney)|D23 Expo]] on [[August 12]], [[2024]].<ref name="D23">{{SW|url=news/d23-brasil-andor-season-2-premiere-date-announce|text=D23 Brasil 2024: ''Andor'' Premiere Date Revealed and Other ''Star Wars'' News}}</ref>

